WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Laid back folk music]

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.875
A few minutes outside Banff, Alberta, there’s a serpentine 
lake,

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.416
Lake Minnewanka.

00:00:10.416 --> 00:00:12.958
It’s a gorgeous lake, perfect for day trips,

00:00:12.958 --> 00:00:16.916
boating, hiking, camping, and even SCUBA diving.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.791
It’s actually a natural lake, but not as it currently 
exists.

00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:24.500
The outlet has been dammed three times, first a small

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.125
timber dam was constructed for flood control in 1895,

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:33.625
replaced with a hydroelectric dam in 1912, with the final and current dam

00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:36.875
and causeway finishing construction in 1941.

00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:42.250
Cumulatively these damming projects have raised the surface of the lake over 25 metres,

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.708
flooding the original shoreline, a small settler town,

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:49.458
and dozens of ancient Stoney Nakoda worksites.

00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:53.333
A number of these old ruins, which you can see marked by 
buoys,

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:56.000
are popular cold water diving destinations.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.625
And if you wanted to demonstrate the curve of the earth

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.000
it would be an ideal place to do it.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.708
So you can see that the water

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:09.875
Clearly has no curvature.

00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:14.708
That the water surface is completely flat.v

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:16.250
Wait, back up.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.166
Why are we demonstrating the curve of the earth?

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:22.833
About five, six years back I got really into Flat Earth 
theories,

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:25.625
not as a believer but as an observer.

00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:28.541
I would check in on them and watch their documentaries

00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:31.041
and read through their memes and infographics and

00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:34.750
generally have a jolly good time poking fun at them on 
Twitter.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.125
I was, at one point, building up to making a

00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:39.416
video on the subject when known moon-criminal

00:01:39.416 --> 00:01:42.083
Hbomberguy produced his video on Flat Earth,

00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:45.250
and due to YouTube Community Standards and bylaws,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.500
section 7.2.1, the Para-Temporal Exclusion Clause,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.625
aka “reviewer dibs”

00:01:51.625 --> 00:01:54.541
I had to shelve my plans for a year and change.

00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:57.166
The thing that really spurred me on originally was

00:01:57.166 --> 00:02:01.166
a specific Flat Earth video I came across one evening in 
2017.

00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:05.166
SubtitleFlat Earth proof 1: the level

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:08.250
Now, this video is not particularly noteworthy

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.500
in the scope of Flat Earth videos.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.166
It’s an hour and a half compilation of short videos

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.666
stolen from a different, smaller Flat Earth YouTube channel.

00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:20.583
It runs through the normal Flat Earth tropes,

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.833
such as not understanding gravity,

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:25.958
failing to appreciate just how big mountains really are,

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:28.791
and generally being really bad at math.

00:02:28.791 --> 00:02:36.041
There was no basis for such an explanation, other than the 
desperate attempt to excuse away these critical findings.

00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:39.666
But there is one thing that makes it special.

00:02:39.666 --> 00:02:42.208
The host of the video does some original research

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:45.000
by going out to the shore of Lake Minnewanka.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.041
Okay, here we are at Lake Minnewanka. In Alberta.

00:02:51.041 --> 00:02:56.666
Thing is, Lake Minnewanka is only 90 minutes away from my 
house.

00:02:56.666 --> 00:03:00.250
The Flat Earth is in my own backyard.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.416
So, hypothetically, if I did want to debunk a forgotten

00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:08.541
four year old Flat Earth video that originally had a couple 
hundred views,

00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:12.250
I could conceivably jump in my car on a clear day,

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.333
drive out to Lake Minnewanka,

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:18.500
and set up a camera with the longest lens I own.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.083
But that’d be ludicrous.

00:03:21.083 --> 00:05:01.583
[Intense music]

00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:08.750
Okay, here we are at Lake Minnewanka. In Alberta.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:19.250
And as you can see we're just less than a foot above the 
water's surface here.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:32.916
And if we zoom in across the lake, the coastline across the 
lake clearly comes into focus.

00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:42.583
So you can see that the water clearly has no curvature.

00:05:42.583 --> 00:05:46.875
That the water surface is completely flat.

00:05:46.875 --> 00:05:51.875
Okay, so, let’s talk real quick about the challenges 
involved in this kind of proof.

00:05:51.875 --> 00:05:55.666
Going out to Minnewanka was actually a really good pick.

00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:59.125
Because the lake is really long there’s a lot of shoreline

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:02.291
where you have several kilometres of unobstructed line of 
sight,

00:06:02.291 --> 00:06:05.416
far enough for the curve of the earth to be meaningful,

00:06:05.416 --> 00:06:10.666
while the mountainous terrain provides a clearly 
identifiable shore on the other side.

00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:14.458
And while the lake is long enough to get these really far 
lines of sight,

00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:19.041
it’s not big enough to get any meaningful tidal movements,

00:06:19.041 --> 00:06:23.000
so all the waves are just from wind blowing across the 
surface,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.958
you don’t get the big, roiling surges that you see in the 
ocean.

00:06:26.958 --> 00:06:30.250
From the dam that makes up the south-west bank of Lake 
Minnewanka

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:33.541
to the rock slide on the far shore where Aylmer canyon meets
 the lake,

00:06:33.541 --> 00:06:36.083
you have a line of sight of seven kilometres,

00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:37.833
about four and a third miles,

00:06:37.833 --> 00:06:42.291
which is far enough that the earth curves away around 3 and 
a half metres,

00:06:42.291 --> 00:06:43.791
or eleven feet.

00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:46.000
This is a kinda perfect distance.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.750
It’s close enough for objects on the far side to still be 
identifiable,

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.375
while being a significant enough curve that the obstruction 
is perceptible.

00:06:55.375 --> 00:06:58.958
If we punch a bunch of numbers into a curvature calculator

00:06:58.958 --> 00:07:02.083
we can see that going from just barely above the water’s 
surface

00:07:02.083 --> 00:07:04.000
to an average adult height,

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.458
the height of a hidden object at 7 kilometres

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:11.166
goes from 3.46 metres to only 0.4 metres.

00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:15.375
This means that something the size of a tree at or near the 
water level of the lake

00:07:15.375 --> 00:07:19.541
should appear just about whole when viewed from a standing 
position,

00:07:19.541 --> 00:07:23.791
but then be visibly obscured by getting down to the surface 
of the water.

00:07:23.791 --> 00:07:25.750
So the experiment should be pretty simple:

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.166
pick a landmark on the far side of the lake

00:07:28.166 --> 00:07:31.375
and record it at the same focal length and distance

00:07:31.375 --> 00:07:34.791
from a couple different elevations above the water’s 
surface.

00:07:34.791 --> 00:07:40.250
Personally I think that his footage does, in fact, show the 
far shore disappearing behind the curve,

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.625
it's just very difficult to tell because the resolution is 
so low.

00:07:44.625 --> 00:07:46.958
So, let’s say, for the sake of argument,

00:07:46.958 --> 00:07:51.500
that an obscure Flat Earth video is still under your skin 
after several years.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.125
What do you do?

00:07:53.125 --> 00:07:56.875
Well, obviously, you throw a bunch of gear into the car,

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:59.833
drive out to the mountains, set up on the side of the lake,

00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:02.333
and spend an hour aiming at a tree on the far shore,

00:08:02.333 --> 00:08:06.250
keeping in mind that if you want to persuade Flat Earthers 
then you need to

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.458
eliminate as much ambiguity as possible,

00:08:09.458 --> 00:08:12.458
so make sure to include an identifiable landmark in the 
shots

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:17.041
to make it easy to pinpoint exactly where you’re standing 
and where you’re looking.

00:08:17.041 --> 00:08:18.708
Everything gets documented:

00:08:18.708 --> 00:08:20.458
where was the camera sitting on the beach,

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:22.458
approximately how high above the surface,

00:08:22.458 --> 00:08:26.291
even screencaps of where GPS says you’re standing.

00:08:26.291 --> 00:08:28.291
You get the footage home, import it,

00:08:28.291 --> 00:08:32.208
tweak the scale to make sure that objects are the same size 
on screen,

00:08:32.208 --> 00:08:34.791
and line it all up with a unified horizon.

00:08:34.791 --> 00:08:38.666
There you go, the tree disappears below the horizon of the 
lake.

00:08:38.666 --> 00:08:39.500
Easy.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:45.291
The earth is round.

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:50.625
Mmm, yeah, but if I were into Flat Earth you know what I’d 
point out?

00:08:50.625 --> 00:08:54.125
That last frame, the one that’s right above the surface of 
the water,

00:08:54.125 --> 00:08:58.416
it’s really hazy, ‘cus it turns out that on a thirty degree 
day

00:08:58.416 --> 00:09:01.583
there’s gonna be a lot of vapour coming off the surface of 
the lake,

00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:04.083
and at water level you’re trying to look

00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:06.916
straight through seven kilometres of the stuff.

00:09:06.916 --> 00:09:11.625
And having such a stark air temperature gradient right at 
the surface of the water

00:09:11.625 --> 00:09:14.083
it increases atmospheric refraction,

00:09:14.083 --> 00:09:17.000
resulting in the mirage effect that allows the pebble beach 
to

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:22.541
occasionally be somewhat visible, despite intersecting the 
tree that it’s below.

00:09:22.541 --> 00:09:26.000
So, you know, a Flat Earther could just dismiss all of this

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.625
as just heat coming off the water.

00:09:28.625 --> 00:09:31.208
And the shots are all locked off and disconnected.

00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:32.750
There’s no continuity.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.125
Who knows what shenanigans you can get up to when the camera
 cuts.

00:09:36.125 --> 00:09:39.458
Plus, I mean, look at it, all that straightening and zooming
 in post,

00:09:39.458 --> 00:09:44.750
how can anyone trust that the camera is set to what you say 
it’s set to?

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:46.541
So!

00:09:46.541 --> 00:09:48.375
Jump back in the car two days later,

00:09:48.375 --> 00:09:50.791
when it’s partly cloudy and fifteen degrees cooler.

00:09:50.791 --> 00:09:54.333
There’s a lot more chop from the wind, but the waves are 
short.

00:09:54.333 --> 00:09:57.291
It’s still a lake, we’re not dealing with big ocean swells.

00:09:57.291 --> 00:10:02.291
Importantly, there’s functionally no visible vapour coming 
off the surface of the water.

00:10:02.291 --> 00:10:05.041
And this time you make sure to bring the jib so you can

00:10:05.041 --> 00:10:10.083
smoothly go from standing to the surface of the water in a 
single motion and…

00:10:10.083 --> 00:11:19.625
[Delicate piano music]

00:11:19.625 --> 00:11:28.291
We checked the footage when we were out there on the lake, 
we looked at it on the camera just to make sure that we got 
something,

00:11:28.291 --> 00:11:32.250
and so we, we knew that we got it but, but

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:42.291
getting home and, and seeing it in, in this detail, like 
this level of clarity

00:11:42.291 --> 00:11:46.666
It's, it's, honestly it's kinda affecting me.

00:11:46.666 --> 00:11:51.250
You know, you can see this just with the naked eye when 
you're out there on the beach.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:12:00.666
You can pick a thing on the far shore and just kinda look at
 it and then like crouch down

00:12:00.666 --> 00:12:09.000
and get like really close to the water's surface and you 
see it get, get occluded but, but

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:15.416
Seeing it at this magnitude, it,

00:12:15.416 --> 00:12:19.708
it feels profound.

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:47.000
[Piano music]

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:52.250
It’s a shame it’s not enough.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:13:00.250
The unfortunate reality of debunking Flat Earth is that it’s
 largely futile,

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:05.416
at least for the actual purpose of persuading Flat Earthers.

00:13:05.416 --> 00:13:07.708
This isn’t me saying that we shouldn’t do it,

00:13:07.708 --> 00:13:11.041
and there are, in fact, a bunch of reasons why we should.

00:13:11.041 --> 00:13:15.916
I mean, first of all, it’s a lot of fun to debunk Flat 
Earth.

00:13:15.916 --> 00:13:20.458
Proving that the earth is round is one of those exercises 
that’s not quite trivial,

00:13:20.458 --> 00:13:25.458
it does take some amount of effort, but it’s not that hard 
either.

00:13:25.458 --> 00:13:27.250
It’s in a really sweet spot.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.250
A lot of it can be done from home with some focused research

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:33.125
or spending the time to do the math properly,

00:13:33.125 --> 00:13:37.416
and other experiments just require living near a relatively 
big lake.

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:42.041
And, yeah, we should admit that it’s a lot of fun to debunk 
a claim like this:

00:13:42.041 --> 00:13:46.416
Another example from Anchorage, Alaska is Mt. McKinley.

00:13:46.416 --> 00:13:54.166
At 130 miles away on the ball earth the 20,320 foot summit 
should be leaning away from the observer

00:13:54.166 --> 00:14:00.208
And almost half covered by 9,220 feet of curved earth.

00:14:00.208 --> 00:14:07.708
But just like Mt. Foraker, Mt. McKinley is always seen 
standing straight up, and visible from base to summit.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:11.041
Okay, we know the distance from Anchorage to Denali,

00:14:11.041 --> 00:14:16.583
it’s 129 miles, which, yes, should create a hidden target 
height of 9000 feet,

00:14:16.583 --> 00:14:20.041
and Denali should be leaning away from the observer,

00:14:20.041 --> 00:14:26.000
but earth has a radius of about 3965 miles and Denali is 
over

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:31.000
twenty thousand feet tall, so at minimum eleven thousand 
feet

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.666
of the mountain should still be visible,

00:14:32.666 --> 00:14:37.958
leaning away from the observer by a trivial 1.8 degrees.

00:14:37.958 --> 00:14:41.625
Like, as a controlled example here are two pyramids in 
Blender.

00:14:41.625 --> 00:14:45.791
One of them is leaning away from the camera by one point 
eight degrees,

00:14:45.791 --> 00:14:48.291
can you tell which one?

00:14:48.291 --> 00:14:51.291
And the base of the mountain cluster on the Anchorage side

00:14:51.291 --> 00:14:54.291
is forty miles closer to the observer than the peak,

00:14:54.291 --> 00:14:57.250
and is 1600 feet above sea level.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:01.625
So the end result is less of the proportional mass of the 
mountain is hidden

00:15:01.625 --> 00:15:06.458
by the curve of the earth than it feels like if you’re just 
looking at the numbers.

00:15:06.458 --> 00:15:10.375
Also you can’t actually see the true base of the mountain 
from Anchorage,

00:15:10.375 --> 00:15:15.041
it just feels like you can because you can see so much of 
the mountain.

00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:18.125
Plus to get a really good look at the mountain you’re 
probably going to

00:15:18.125 --> 00:15:20.000
have to find some higher elevation yourself,

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:24.375
just to see over buildings, trees, hills, and other nearby 
obstructions,

00:15:24.375 --> 00:15:28.666
which will further increase your line of sight over the 
curve.

00:15:28.666 --> 00:15:37.583
Like just in this example here, we can see over the tallest 
buildings in Anchorage, so the photograph was taken from at 
least 300 feet up.

00:15:37.583 --> 00:15:42.625
Bottom line is you can see Denali from very far away because
 it’s

00:15:42.625 --> 00:15:47.958
really, really, really, really big,

00:15:47.958 --> 00:15:52.625
and it was the pyramid on the right that was leaning awayv.

00:15:52.625 --> 00:15:54.375
That’s fun to figure out.

00:15:54.375 --> 00:15:58.000
It’s the same kind of satisfaction you get from solving a 
math puzzle.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:02.250
Or something like this, claiming that there are no 
south-pointing compasses,

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:05.916
that’s a fantastic starter for talking about how we 
privilege the

00:16:05.916 --> 00:16:12.791
global north in science in small but consistent ways, via 
maps or, yes, things like compasses.

00:16:12.791 --> 00:16:19.083
Because, like, every compass is a south-pointing compass, 
but we don't frame it that way.

00:16:19.083 --> 00:16:24.875
We paint one arm of the compass red and say that that points
 north

00:16:24.875 --> 00:16:30.458
and we talk abut compasses in those terms, we say that, it's
 like, oh, this indicates north.

00:16:30.458 --> 00:16:36.625
Even though what it's really doing is it's aligning itself 
with the directionality of the magnetic field

00:16:36.625 --> 00:16:46.041
So it's indicating both north and south, it's indicating 
polarity, and points towards both poles simultaneously,

00:16:46.041 --> 00:16:50.333
but that's not the language that we use to describe it.

00:16:50.333 --> 00:16:53.541
And driving out to the mountains with a trunk full of camera
 gear,

00:16:53.541 --> 00:16:57.208
spending an afternoon sitting on the shore of a gorgeous 
lake,

00:16:57.208 --> 00:16:59.291
that’s just a lot of fun,

00:16:59.291 --> 00:17:03.833
and you get a chance to show everyone something really cool 
about our world.

00:17:03.833 --> 00:17:08.750
And sometimes Flat Earthers are just hilarious.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:14.875
All the movies about space and all the other movies, they 
all in some way push that globe model

00:17:14.875 --> 00:17:17.291
The globe, the image of the Beast.

00:17:17.291 --> 00:17:22.500
Heliocentrism has nothing to do with science!

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:27.791
The idea that the sun is the centre was thought up by 
occultists.

00:17:27.791 --> 00:17:30.166
Jesuit priests.

00:17:30.166 --> 00:17:31.541
The Vatican.

00:17:31.541 --> 00:17:34.208
It's not, it has nothing to do with science.

00:17:34.208 --> 00:17:42.791
And they say that the earth orbits the sun going 66,600 
miles an hour.

00:17:42.791 --> 00:17:57.333
And if you Google how fast does the earth orbit the sun they
 tell you 18.5 miles per second

00:17:57.333 --> 00:17:59.458
[bong noise]

00:17:59.458 --> 00:18:01.500
Hold on I'm taking a hit

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.375
And that’s honestly the frame that most Flat Earth debunking
 lives within.

00:18:05.375 --> 00:18:10.000
The nonsense claims of Flat Earthers form the starting point
 of a process of

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.416
puzzle solving or discussion of geography or a mini lesson 
in optics,

00:18:14.416 --> 00:18:21.333
because, at the end of the day, Flat Earthers are not 
available to be persuaded.

00:18:21.333 --> 00:18:23.375
[bell noises]

00:18:23.375 --> 00:18:30.666
So, we do need to be really careful while we're out here, 
this is bear country. Not just bear country, this is serious
 bear country.

00:18:30.666 --> 00:18:43.250
So we got bear bells, we got bear spray, and the thing is 
that right now we're at the tail end of their fall, like,

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:49.041
feeding season, when they get really, when they stock up for
 winter,

00:18:49.041 --> 00:18:57.333
and around the lake and up into a couple of these canyons 
here is prime growing area for,

00:18:57.333 --> 00:19:04.000
for the bison berries that they, that they eat to do it.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.250
And at this point we should talk about what Flat Earth is.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:11.083
Like, what Flat Earth really is.

00:19:11.083 --> 00:19:15.375
Nominally Flat Earth is a belief that the earth isn’t a 
globe,

00:19:15.375 --> 00:19:19.333
but is actually flat, a fact that has been kept from Us,

00:19:19.333 --> 00:19:21.208
meaning normal people,

00:19:21.208 --> 00:19:26.583
by a nebulous, powerful Them for nefarious, inscrutable 
purposes.

00:19:26.583 --> 00:19:29.916
This is where profiles of Flat Earth tend to stop.

00:19:29.916 --> 00:19:33.500
Which is fair, it’s a reasonable summary for most purposes.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.375
I want to go beyond that, though, because I think it’s worth
 considering

00:19:37.375 --> 00:19:43.541
that the shape of the earth might actually be the least 
important belief of Flat Earth.

00:19:43.541 --> 00:19:49.125
Flat Earth is a syncretic Biblical belief that is both 
evangelical and apocalyptic.

00:19:49.125 --> 00:19:51.833
That’s a lot of jargon, what does that mean?

00:19:51.833 --> 00:19:54.958
Syncretism is effectively a process of creating

00:19:54.958 --> 00:19:58.916
new texts out of the desirable parts of old texts,

00:19:58.916 --> 00:20:02.208
regardless of the previous relationship between those texts.

00:20:02.208 --> 00:20:06.041
Syncretism is saying two different books both mention 
dragons

00:20:06.041 --> 00:20:09.750
or use the word dragon or call an antagonist “The Great 
Dragon”,

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.125
so they must be referring to the same thing,

00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:14.958
they’re talking about the exact same Great Dragon,

00:20:14.958 --> 00:20:18.291
and if we cobble together all these different stories of 
dragons

00:20:18.291 --> 00:20:21.333
we can uncover the truth about dragons.

00:20:21.333 --> 00:20:29.166
The finger pointing at the now defunct NASA will then turn 
to finger pointing at the government, who directed the whole
 thing.

00:20:29.166 --> 00:20:37.625
This is where we run into some dangerous ground involving 
things like the Arc of the Covenant, the Holy Grail, and the
 Ring of Power.

00:20:37.625 --> 00:20:42.000
As a syncretic belief system you’ll find all sorts of 
fragmentary elements

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.666
lifted from seemingly disconnected and often contradictory 
sources,

00:20:45.666 --> 00:20:49.041
forced into something resembling agreement,

00:20:49.041 --> 00:20:53.458
and this spans various legitimate ancient texts as well as 
modern myths.

00:20:53.458 --> 00:20:58.958
Angels, giants, world trees, and modern conspiracy staples 
like MK-Ultra,

00:20:58.958 --> 00:21:01.666
the Kennedy assassination, and aliens all

00:21:01.666 --> 00:21:05.125
have a spot at the table in some corner or another.

00:21:28.333 --> 00:21:32.041
Additionally support will be teased out of nearly any sacred
 text

00:21:32.041 --> 00:21:35.541
that is sufficiently mythological or abstract,

00:21:35.541 --> 00:21:39.375
such that it can be stripped of context or interpreted 
hyper-literally

00:21:39.375 --> 00:21:44.875
or in some way be made to agree with the construction of 
their reality.

00:22:02.833 --> 00:22:07.958
Also I should note that I’m specifically framing this as a 
syncretic Biblical belief,

00:22:07.958 --> 00:22:12.000
not strictly Christian, because while the modern Flat Earth 
movement

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:17.083
clearly has deep roots in the social and lexical traditions 
of American Christianity,

00:22:17.083 --> 00:22:23.833
the actual theological doctrines of Christianity are largely
 absent or secularized.

00:22:23.833 --> 00:22:29.291
While the Bible is a core text, and many Flat Earth 
evangelists are unambiguously Christian,

00:22:29.291 --> 00:22:33.583
the wider Flat Earth movement is largely only

00:22:33.583 --> 00:22:37.250
interested in the parts concerning the creation and end of 
the world.

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:42.041
In essence modern Flat Earth is an offshoot of Christianity 
where Jesus

00:22:42.041 --> 00:22:46.958
is a secondary figure and the primary theological concern is
 the true

00:22:46.958 --> 00:22:51.041
nature of the physical world, its origin, and its destiny.

00:22:51.041 --> 00:22:55.541
But, also, all that lives side by side with pop culture 
Egyptology,

00:22:55.541 --> 00:23:03.500
mystical Gnosticism, and, I dunno what you’d call it, 
esoteric fictionalism,

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:09.291
this belief that the fantastical worlds of pop culture are a
 warped or

00:23:09.291 --> 00:23:12.333
coded reflection of the true world.

00:23:20.375 --> 00:23:24.583
It’s chaotic and inconsistent because there is no central 
authority,

00:23:24.583 --> 00:23:29.541
no unique unifying texts, so you’ll find different 
commentators that take

00:23:29.541 --> 00:23:34.083
any given point to more or less extreme conclusions, which 
can make it

00:23:34.083 --> 00:23:38.375
difficult to talk about the movement as a whole, but there 
are elements

00:23:38.375 --> 00:23:42.500
that remain consistent across the field of Flat Earth texts.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:46.833
The world is flat and “they” are hiding that fact from you 
because a

00:23:46.833 --> 00:23:53.333
Flat Earth would be irrefutable proof that we live in a 
divine fishbowl, and thus god is real.

00:23:53.333 --> 00:23:57.750
This is important because, again, they are evangelical and 
apocalyptic.

00:23:57.750 --> 00:24:02.125
This means, first, that orthodoxy is considered a spiritual 
necessity,

00:24:02.125 --> 00:24:07.041
that there is a universal divine moral right and wrong, and 
all are

00:24:07.041 --> 00:24:09.583
held to account for the rightness of their beliefs.

00:24:09.583 --> 00:24:13.750
As a result it is the imperative of the believers to make 
sure as many

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:19.000
people are believers as possible because there are 
consequences for not believing.

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:28.125
To be clear, and I can't stress this enough, do not start 
conversations with the word 'flat earth'

00:24:28.125 --> 00:24:32.166
You may note, already, that this is clearly setting up an 
adversarial

00:24:32.166 --> 00:24:37.000
relationship between Flat Earthers and everyone else, as 
anyone who denies

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:42.125
Flat Earth or works to debunk it is not just presenting 
alternative evidence

00:24:42.125 --> 00:24:46.583
of the way the world works, but is impeding proof of god.

00:24:46.583 --> 00:24:50.000
The second critical meaning is a belief that there is an 
impending

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:52.416
literal end to the world.

00:24:52.416 --> 00:24:55.750
This end will occur at some unknown point in the future,

00:24:55.750 --> 00:25:00.750
but that point is always “soon”. Many Flat Earthers 
subscribe to the pop culture

00:25:00.750 --> 00:25:02.708
version of a Biblical apocalypse,

00:25:02.708 --> 00:25:05.875
but it doesn’t actually feature very heavily for the most 
part,

00:25:05.875 --> 00:25:13.166
with most skipping past the details to the part where god 
shows up and proves they're right.

00:25:13.166 --> 00:25:16.916
It is difficult to understate the impact on long term 
planning,

00:25:16.916 --> 00:25:19.583
the support for policies and politicians,

00:25:19.583 --> 00:25:23.625
that comes from the belief that at some point in the next 
generation or two

00:25:23.625 --> 00:25:27.750
God will just personally show up and wrap up humanity,

00:25:27.750 --> 00:25:30.625
like a board game being packed back into its box.

00:25:30.625 --> 00:25:35.625
A critical component of Flat Earth’s worldview is the 
baked-in idea of opposition.

00:25:35.625 --> 00:25:40.625
The enemy, the “them”, isn’t merely another group with a 
different idea

00:25:40.625 --> 00:25:43.875
of what’s best for the world, or a different set of 
motivations

00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:47.208
that may or may not intersect with the wellbeing of others,

00:25:47.208 --> 00:25:49.875
they are actively seeking harm.

00:25:49.875 --> 00:25:54.208
This is, in a way, the immune response of paranoid 
conspiratorial thought.

00:25:54.208 --> 00:25:57.708
It creates an impenetrable counter to any conflict.

00:25:57.708 --> 00:26:02.875
Any disagreement, any counter-argument, is clearly 
manufactured by an opposition

00:26:02.875 --> 00:26:09.333
that isn’t merely indifferent to truth, but actively, 
knowingly suppressing it.

00:26:09.333 --> 00:26:13.708
I wanted to take a look at this dimension of Flat Earth 
because two of my peers and friends,

00:26:13.708 --> 00:26:17.708
H.bomberguy and Philosophy Tube, have done videos on Flat 
Earth

00:26:17.708 --> 00:26:24.166
and while I don’t think they are wrong, I think their 
assessment of Flat Earth is incomplete.

00:26:24.166 --> 00:26:29.458
Both of their videos function, like many others, by taking 
Flat Earth as a jumping off point

00:26:29.458 --> 00:26:36.333
to discuss intersecting concepts of philosophy and science 
and sociology, and that’s great.

00:26:36.333 --> 00:26:37.875
They’re good videos.

00:26:37.875 --> 00:26:42.875
The idea that Philosophy Tube brings up, that discussions of
 science are a rhetorical exercise,

00:26:42.875 --> 00:26:47.875
influenced by the social context that they are had within,

00:26:47.875 --> 00:26:52.875
and the idea that Flat Earthers are unpersuaded by 
conventional rhetoric,

00:26:52.875 --> 00:26:57.875
or perhaps persuaded into Flat Earth by unconventional 
rhetoric,

00:26:57.875 --> 00:27:00.375
is one that we have grappled with in making this,

00:27:00.375 --> 00:27:02.708
it is an extremely relevant concept.

00:27:02.708 --> 00:27:04.583
None of those have

00:27:04.583 --> 00:27:05.833
anything whatsoever to do with the

00:27:05.833 --> 00:27:08.041
evidence they just

00:27:08.041 --> 00:27:11.750
all note a failure to be rhetorically persuaded

00:27:11.750 --> 00:27:16.208
Harry goes to great lengths to give Flat Earthers the 
benefit of the doubt,

00:27:16.208 --> 00:27:20.291
carefully isolating the very specific belief that that world
 is flat

00:27:20.291 --> 00:27:24.000
and addressing the anxieties that specifically,

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:27.791
narrowly come up with the ontology of the physical world.

00:27:27.791 --> 00:27:33.125
you're right to feel that something is wrong

00:27:33.125 --> 00:27:35.208
because something is wrong just maybe

00:27:35.208 --> 00:27:37.583
keep looking for the source of what that

00:27:37.583 --> 00:27:39.708
thing is because

00:27:39.708 --> 00:27:40.750
the earth is not flat.

00:27:40.750 --> 00:27:45.875
On the surface Flat Earthers share many of the same 
anxieties as the rest of us:

00:27:45.875 --> 00:27:50.875
they are worried about the power structures that have 
immense influence over our lives,

00:27:50.875 --> 00:27:54.833
the systems that shape the information we have access to,

00:27:54.833 --> 00:27:58.166
and the shared fictions that society operates on

00:27:58.166 --> 00:28:00.000
like money and rent.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.250
But there is, perhaps, an over-willingness to treat them as 
harmless cranks,

00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:08.083
as though we can start from their shared frustrations with 
the world,

00:28:08.083 --> 00:28:12.583
and just gently nudge them in a more sensible direction.

00:28:12.583 --> 00:28:16.875
These common anxieties are a shared coordinate that is, I 
think,

00:28:16.875 --> 00:28:20.375
far more superficial than we would want it to be,

00:28:20.375 --> 00:28:25.041
because while we’re all worried and skeptical of what people
 in power are doing,

00:28:25.041 --> 00:28:29.958
Flat Earthers have very, very different ideas about who’s in
 power

00:28:29.958 --> 00:28:32.125
and what they’re trying to do with it.

00:28:32.125 --> 00:28:37.583
Flat Earthers are not otherwise empty vessels who believe 
one kooky thing.

00:28:37.583 --> 00:28:41.250
They believe that thing because it suits their purposes.

00:28:41.250 --> 00:28:44.250
Flat Earthers have an agenda.

00:28:44.250 --> 00:28:48.416
The end goal of conspiratorial beliefs is to simplify 
reality

00:28:48.416 --> 00:28:51.291
by attributing the high-chaos state of the world to a

00:28:51.291 --> 00:28:56.041
singular active force or group opposed by an equally 
singular solution.

00:28:56.041 --> 00:28:58.208
indoctrination is the way they run this

00:28:58.208 --> 00:28:59.708
world it's the way that they keep their

00:28:59.708 --> 00:29:01.250
lie going

00:29:01.250 --> 00:29:03.250
it's the way that they have passed their

00:29:03.250 --> 00:29:05.000
lie along as science when it is nothing

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.000
more than a belief

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:09.375
they have a biased foundation built on a

00:29:09.375 --> 00:29:11.291
lie and now they know they're stuck

00:29:11.291 --> 00:29:14.666
Their anxiety is that the world has become too complex,

00:29:14.666 --> 00:29:16.916
that too many things are changing,

00:29:16.916 --> 00:29:20.291
and that science and progressivism are actively malicious 
elements

00:29:20.291 --> 00:29:23.708
working to obstruct the true nature of god.

00:29:23.708 --> 00:29:28.708
Most people don’t actually believe Flat Earth because they 
were persuaded by shoddy evidence,

00:29:28.708 --> 00:29:33.708
or they found other evidence to be less persuasive about the
 nature of the physical world,

00:29:33.708 --> 00:29:41.250
they do so because it says something they already believe 
about the nature of the social world.

00:29:41.250 --> 00:29:46.250
Flat Earth is a thing people want to believe because if it 
were true

00:29:46.250 --> 00:29:50.291
it would be irrefutable proof of everything else they 
believe.

00:29:50.291 --> 00:29:54.583
Flat Earth is a system that selectively delegitimizes power 
structures

00:29:54.583 --> 00:29:56.916
and does so by working backwards.

00:29:56.916 --> 00:30:00.333
Flat Earth insists that you are being lied to by “them”,

00:30:00.333 --> 00:30:02.833
typically gays, liberals, or jews,

00:30:02.833 --> 00:30:07.208
in order to obfuscate the existence of God and are thus not 
merely

00:30:07.208 --> 00:30:14.250
an opponent of their isolationist, xenophobic policies but 
an enemy of righteousness itself.

00:30:14.250 --> 00:30:18.125
heliocentrism is simply modern day sun worship

00:30:18.125 --> 00:30:20.375
masquerading as a science

00:30:20.375 --> 00:30:26.166
They are not trying to explain the world, they are 
attempting to un-explain it,

00:30:26.166 --> 00:30:33.500
because those explanations, the real explanations, have 
become inconvenient to their politics.

00:30:33.500 --> 00:30:38.208
And while there is a shared sense of the world being out of 
whack,

00:30:38.208 --> 00:30:42.583
the diagnosis and prescriptions are very different.

00:30:42.583 --> 00:30:48.666
I don’t think it’s actually possible to isolate Flat Earth 
from the reactionary current that it swims in and,

00:30:48.666 --> 00:30:50.500
I dunno,

00:30:50.500 --> 00:30:54.083
for some reason in 2020 I’ve found myself with a lot less 
patience for

00:30:54.083 --> 00:30:57.791
people who engage in performative rejection of empathy and 
evidence.

00:30:57.791 --> 00:31:02.083
On that note, who wants to guess how Flat Earthers feel 
about COVID masks?

00:31:02.083 --> 00:31:04.083
anyone that is voluntarily wearing a

00:31:04.083 --> 00:31:07.208
mask at this stage

00:31:07.208 --> 00:31:08.791
is a mindless drone who couldn't think

00:31:08.791 --> 00:31:11.208
for themselves if their

00:31:11.208 --> 00:31:13.541
life depended on it

00:31:13.541 --> 00:31:17.000
The deeper, more critical issue is in the information 
landscape

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:20.083
that has given rise to new faith movements like Flat Earth.

00:31:20.083 --> 00:31:24.750
We are in an extremely low-trust media environment as a 
product of

00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:28.166
decades of active sabotage combined with a corporate,

00:31:28.166 --> 00:31:32.291
capitalist environment that prioritizes the interests of the
 wealthy

00:31:32.291 --> 00:31:36.416
or blindly pursues metric-driven success models like 
“engagement”.

00:31:36.416 --> 00:31:42.875
There are a lot of legitimate reasons to distrust the media,
 to see them as at-best spineless

00:31:42.875 --> 00:31:47.708
in the face of disinformation or as outright collaborators 
and profiteers.

00:31:47.708 --> 00:31:52.708
The prevalence of legitimate reasons for distrust, 
legitimate anxieties for the future,

00:31:52.708 --> 00:31:56.875
creates an ideal environment for groups like Flat Earth who 
peddle

00:31:56.875 --> 00:32:00.208
a simplistic Us vs. Them model of the universe.

